  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "After running fedora-rebuild, the pidGen tables sometimes isn't populated.  This can cause an error when ingesting objects where the pid is unspecified and must be auto-generated.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The workaround is to check this table after a rebuild and, if it is unpopulated, issue the following SQL before restarting Fedora:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "INSERT INTO pidGen (namespace, highestID)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "VALUES ($NS, $HIGHESTID)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Where $NS is the namespace, such as \"demo\",",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and highestID is the higest existing numeric",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "part of all PIDs in the repository, such as 10.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
