     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: cwilper<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=189298<br/>\nOriginator: YES</p>\n\n<p>This was caused by clearing the tables <b>after</b> the RebuildServer had started as part of the rebuild process.  The value of the last generated PID in memory differed from that in the database, and this cause the behavior to occur when the pidGen table was populated prior to running a rebuild.  The behavior wouldn't occur if the pidGen table was empty prior to a rebuild, because the value in memory would not be out of sync with the value in the db (both empty).</p>\n\n<p>The solution was to change the beginning of the SQL rebuild process so that the tables were cleared BEFORE the RebuildServer was started.</p>\n\n<p>The change has been committed to the maintenance-2.2 branch as well as the trunk.</p>",
