  "description": "<p>After running fedora-rebuild, the pidGen tables sometimes isn't populated.  This can cause an error when ingesting objects where the pid is unspecified and must be auto-generated.</p>\n\n<p>The workaround is to check this table after a rebuild and, if it is unpopulated, issue the following SQL before restarting Fedora:</p>\n\n<p>INSERT INTO pidGen (namespace, highestID)<br/>\nVALUES ($NS, $HIGHESTID)</p>\n\n<p>Where $NS is the namespace, such as \"demo\",<br/>\nand highestID is the higest existing numeric<br/>\npart of all PIDs in the repository, such as 10.</p>",
